      "writtenOn": "2019-12-16T14:36:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think all this BigInteger arithmetic is easier to understand than a simple loop.\n\n  byte endAddr[] \u003d startAddr.getAddress();\n  for (int bitIndex \u003d prefixLen; bitIndex \u003c 8 * endAddr.length; ++bitIndex) {\n    endAddr[bitIndex \u003e\u003e 3] |\u003d 0x80 \u003e\u003e (bitIndex % 8);\n  }\n\nWhile this is not very very fast and could be improved with constants, it is still much faster than your arithmetic, and I would argue easier to understand and easier to comment. It\u0027s also three lines to compare to your 40 (counting functions). You can optionally make a function to return the 0x80 \u003e\u003e (bitIndex % 8) if you find this easier to think about, and replace bitIndex \u003e\u003e 3 with bitIndex / 8 if you find this easier.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 74,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 74,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "bee5d5d38f9ffa8aa918eb6eff3f4ccfb9ece063",
